SUMMARY:The finitary aspects of Full Ground Local State (Orpheas van Rooij 
 (University of Edinburgh))
LOCATION:LG23\, Computer Science
DESCRIPTION:Orpheas van Rooij (University of Edinburgh)\nTheoretical Comput
 er Science Seminar\n\nFull ground local state (FGLS) refers to dynamically
  allocated mutable state that allows storing ground values and references.
  It is a key ingredient in many imperative algorithms as it enables cyclic
  data structures. In this work\, we focus on one particular denotational m
 odel for FGLS: Kammar et al.'s possible worlds monad on sets indexed over 
 sets of locations. We resolve an outstanding question about this FGLS mona
 d: is it finitary? We show that it is not\, by showing the existence of no
 n-finitary computations in this monad that are challenging to define in a 
 terminating language with full ground references. This prompts us to intro
 duce a finitary submonad of Kammar et al.'s monad\, which…\n\nDetails: h
 ttps://researchseminars.org/talk/TheoryCSBham/90/
